---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="From engineering intent to working systems">
  <p class="eyebrow">Executable Engineering Lab</p>
  <h1>From engineering intent to working systems.</h1>
  <p class="lead">An industrial area needs monitoring. What would count as enough coverage—and what would convince you that a proposed configuration provides it?</p>
  <p>Work through one engineering question using a fictional monitoring system: define a criterion, experiment with a single-sensor model, and judge what its evidence actually establishes.</p>
  <p class="lead"><a href={`${base}learn/01-engineering-intent/`}>Start Chapter 1: From Engineering Intent to Evidence →</a></p>
  <section class="cards" aria-label="Learning path">
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Ask</p><h2>Define success</h2><p>Separate the operator’s need from the measurable criterion and the assumptions behind it.</p><a href={`${base}learn/01-engineering-intent/`}>Read Chapter 1</a></article>
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Experiment</p><h2>Explore the model</h2><p>Vary one sensor’s radius and position. Compare configurations against the same requirement.</p><a href={`${base}lab/`}>Open the lab</a></article>
    <article class="card"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Inspect</p><h2>Examine the evidence</h2><p>Follow the requirement to its scenario, executable model, test and retained verification record.</p><a href={`${base}reference/`}>Inspect engineering sources</a></article>
  </section>
  <p>This first lesson uses an idealized geometric area estimate. A passing result does not establish real-world detection performance or an optimal design.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab#readme">Reproduce the calculation locally</a> · <a href="https://github.com/And-Gu/executable-engineering-lab/blob/main/ROADMAP.md">Later learning increments</a></p>
</Layout>
